<title>ANTIGUA: CRICKET-WEST INDIES KEEP SAME SQUAD FOR SECOND TEST.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-WEST INDIES KEEP SAME SQUAD FOR SECOND TEST.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOHN'S, Antigua 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>West Indies have named an unchanged squad of 13 for the second test against India starting in Port of Spain, Trinidad, on Friday.</p>
<p>The first test in the five-match series ended in a draw at Kingston, Jamaica, on Monday.</p>
<p>Squad: Courtney Walsh (captain), Sherwin Campbell, Stuart Williams, Shivnarine Chanderpaul, Brian Lara, Carl Hooper, Roland Holder, Jimmy Adams, Junior Murray, Ian Bishop, Curtly Ambrose, Franklyn Rose, Rawl Lewis.</p>
